so that's the version I rolled back to.\n- The first rollback attempt failed partway because of an orchestrator error. Only us-east switched to v2.3.0, while us-west and eu-west stayed on v2.3.1.\n- I ran the same rollback again and it finished in all regions. us-east, us-west and eu-west now all run v2.3.0.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to create the SEV2 incident timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and saw it had been created anyway. I didn't resend it, to avoid a duplicate incident and a second page to on-call.\n- It records what happened, the partial rollback and retry, the current state, and three follow-ups:\n  - Find out what broke v2.3.1.\n  - Find out what caused the orchestrator error during the rollback.\n  - Find out why v2.3.1 was released to production when its test build (v2.3.1-rc) was also unhealthy in staging.", "type": "text"}]}]}